**Known for**: SerenityOS, Ladybird

**Alias**: AwesomeKling

Andreas is the founder of SerenityOS and the Ladybird web browser. He posted in
support of Charlie Kirk after his assassination,[[source]][0] gets triggered by
the phrase "punch nazis",[[source]][1] and the idea of using gender-neutral
pronouns in documentation.[[source]][2] Andreas boosted [David Heinemeier
Hansson]($link.page('weird-guys').unsafeRef('dhh'))'s tweets on DEI and the
white supremacist "white replacement" theory,[[source]][3] and expressed
solidarity with David's persecution for his "banal, mainstream" positions,
positions which include, for example, the forced expulsion of non-white people
from Europe.[[source]][4]

Ladybird and Andreas have received sponsorships from FUTO, Cloudflare, Shopify
and 37signals (i.e. David Heinemeier Hansson), Proton, Jetbrains, Sourcegraph,
and others.[[source]][5]

